{"title":"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A spinner was created by drawing five radii from the centre of a circle. The first four radii divide the circle into four equal wedges. The fifth radius divides one of the wedges into two parts, one having twice the area of the other. The five wedges are labelled as pictured with the wedge labeled by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> having twice the area of the wedge labeled by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Determine the probability of spinning an odd number. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can split the problem into two different cases: one where the spinner lands on either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and another where the spinner lands on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, since those are the odd numbers on the spinner.\n</p><p>For the first case, the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/a/dbaa7bcbcc129e8efc76dbce04421b1047eb3577.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> quarters of the circle are covered by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>For the second case, the spinner must land in the top right quarter. This would have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> probability. Given that we landed in the top right corner, the probability of getting a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> because the probability of getting a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the probability of getting a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and both sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>This means that the probability of getting a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13f5aafaaf5654b8685125fe901189907865595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\times \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the probability of getting an odd is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/473694a742abee851954b2dbd045e084df86034d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{4} + \\frac{1}{12} = \\frac{2 \\times 3}{4 \\times 3} + \\frac{1}{12} = \\frac{6}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"219\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17fbb294f623fa4c938f5709e7be02ceba33ac33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{1 + 6}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"65\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59efaa4f4dd4d72f912e55181ae1fe39648d5b08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed{\\frac{7}{12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"54\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since all of the numbers on the spinner are integers, getting an odd number would be the same as getting something that wasn't an even number. Thus, we can subtract the probability of getting an even number from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get the probability of getting an odd number.\n</p><p>We can split the problem into two different cases: one where the spinner lands on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and another where the spinner lands on a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> since those are the even numbers on the spinner.\n</p><p>For the first case, the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> quarter of the circle is covered by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>For the second case, the spinner must land in the top right quarter. This would have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> probability. Given that we landed in the top right corner, the probability of getting a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> because the probability of getting a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the probability of getting a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and both sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>This means that the probability of getting a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d3ee908b97d946ac870d8f529e2719985e2231.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\times \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{2}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the probability of getting an even is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/d/42d54c559146726053d2e52a6db2a854d1e96785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{2}{12} = \\frac{1 \\times 3}{4 \\times 3} + \\frac{2}{12} = \\frac{3}{12} + \\frac{2}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"263\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/8/998ef71ed37f70f56119c1647196470f90bbf0ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{3 + 2}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"65\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd1d9e7736c81e34b57d847b292fba73ee12338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{5}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"43\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The probability of getting an odd is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/8/288bd2e9f32038150fbb8be5804728476be57df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\frac{5}{12} = \\boxed {\\frac{7}{12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"113\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC\">2020 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Individual Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Individual Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_1\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 1\">Individual 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 2\">Individual 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Individual 3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Individual 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Individual 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_6\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 6\">Individual 6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_7\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 7\">Individual 7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Individual 8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Individual 9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Individual 10</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_A\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem A\">Relay 1 A</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_B\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem B\">Relay 1 B</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_C\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem C\">Relay 1 C</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_2_Problem_A&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 2 Problem A (page does not exist)\">Relay 2 A</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_2_Problem_B&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 2 Problem B (page does not exist)\">Relay 2 B</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_CTMC_Problems